This package includes material from the following projects.

src/library/volviewPresets.ts
  The transfer function presets of VolView (src/vtk/MedicalColorPresets.json), copied as data.
  https://github.com/Kitware/VolView
  Copyright Kitware, Inc. Apache License 2.0.

src/library/colorMaps.ts
  Colour maps from vtk.js (Sources/Rendering/Core/ColorTransferFunction/ColorMaps.json), resampled.
  https://github.com/Kitware/vtk-js
  Copyright (c) 2016, Kitware Inc. BSD 3-Clause License.
  viridis, magma, inferno and plasma are the matplotlib colour maps by Nathaniel J. Smith, Stefan van der Walt and
  Eric Firing, released as CC0: https://bids.github.io/colormap/

src/shaders/volume.frag.glsl
  volNoise: interleaved gradient noise, Jorge Jimenez, "Next Generation Post Processing in Call of Duty: Advanced
  Warfare", SIGGRAPH 2014.
  The ray-box test, back-face ray setup and camera-inside handling follow the three.js volume examples
  (examples/webgl_volume_cloud.html) and VolumeNodeMaterial, https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js, MIT License.

src/loaders/NRRDLoadPlugin.ts, src/VolumeData.ts
  Use three.js NRRDLoader and Volume (examples/jsm), https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js, MIT License.

src/derived/EmptySpaceMap.ts, src/shaders/volume.frag.glsl
  Empty space skipping with a Chebyshev distance map follows the method of L. J. Deakin and M. A. Knackstedt,
  "Accelerated volume rendering with Chebyshev distance maps", SIGGRAPH Asia 2019 Technical Briefs (no code copied).

src/shaders/volume.frag.glsl (lighting)
  The surface, volume and hybrid shading models follow vtk.js (Sources/Rendering/OpenGL/glsl/vtkVolumeFS.glsl):
  https://github.com/Kitware/vtk-js, Copyright (c) 2016, Kitware Inc., BSD 3-Clause License; and Exposure Render,
  T. Kroes, F. H. Post and C. P. Botha, "Exposure Render: An Interactive Photo-Realistic Volume Rendering Framework",
  PLoS ONE 2012 (method). volSpecularGGX ports BRDF_GGX of three.js (lights_physical_pars_fragment), MIT License.
  volSample with VOL_CUBIC: C. Sigg and M. Hadwiger, "Fast Third-Order Texture Filtering", GPU Gems 2, 2005 (method).

src/derived/LightVolume.ts
  Light propagation by slices follows T. Ropinski, C. Doring and C. Rezk-Salama, "Interactive Volumetric Lighting
  Simulating Scattering and Shadowing", IEEE PacificVis 2010 (method, no code copied).

src/VolumePlugin.ts
  Spherical harmonics of the environment with three.js LightProbeGenerator (examples/jsm), MIT License.

src/procedural.ts
  volHash and volHash3: "Hash without Sine" by Dave Hoskins, https://www.shadertoy.com/view/4djSRW, MIT License.

src/shaders/volume.frag.glsl (volScatter)
  Multiple scattering by octaves follows M. Wrenninge, "Art-Directable Multiple Volumetric Scattering", SIGGRAPH 2015
  Talks, as used in S. Hillaire, "Physically Based Sky, Atmosphere and Cloud Rendering in Frostbite", 2016 (method).

src/library/transferFormats.ts
  The .clut reader and writer port MRIcroGL colorTable.pas (CLUT2disk, GenerateLUT), https://github.com/rordenlab/MRIcroGL,
  Copyright (c) 2014-2019 Chris Rorden, BSD 3-Clause License. The NiiVue colour map shape is from NiiVue,
  https://github.com/niivue/niivue, BSD 2-Clause License.
